n our radar since his  masterful debut the return back in 2003  number four coming home directed by John  emo the story of a Chinese man who is  forced into marriage and flees to  America but when he returns home is sent  to a labor camp Li Gong and Chun dal  mean star in this heavy period piece  number three winter sleep written and  directed by Nuri bilge jalan-jalan spree  vyas film once upon a time in Anatolia  won the Grand Jury Prize at kin in 2011  plot details for winter sleep are a tad  scarce we're trusting Jalen and his past  collaborators on this one which happens  to be the longest film in competition  this year at 3 hours and 16 minutes  number two Foxcatcher directed by  banette Miller Miller of Capote and  Moneyball fame has a recognized gift for  bringing true stories of misunderstood  men to the big screen next in line is  paranoid schizophrenic John du Pont  whose life collided with the Olympic  wrestling duo the Schultz Brothers it's  Steve Carell and the role of DuPont that  has piqued our interests ever since the  film was first revealed and we look  forward to him acting opposite Channing  Tatum and Mark Ruffalo number one the  homesman written and directed by Tommy  Lee Jones with the homesman he plays a  claim-jumper opposite a pioneer woman  played by Hilary Swank who team up to  escort three mentally insane women from  Nebraska to Iowa we've never seen a  roadtrip movie like this before after  seeing the trailer for the homesman we  found ourselves wishing that Tommy Lee  Jones would just make westerns for the  rest of his career those are our top 10  most anticipated films for the 2014  Cannes Film Festival keep a tab open on  the movieclips Film Festival channel for  trailers clips and more and as always  thanks for watching  you  [Music]
 

